From d5deb283bbebeeb9cef8dfd7dd03991b2ce64fa0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:27:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-302: IQ4_NL gather K-tail redistribution, opt-in
 GGML_ARIFI_MOE_GATHER_TAIL=1 (=2 planted wrong arm)

IQ4_NL down has K=640; on a 64-lane subgroup with 8 values per lane the last K iteration ran 16 of 64 lanes.
Each lane now computes one owner's tail chunk for one row (16 chunks x 4 rows = 64) and the owner pulls it by
subgroupShuffle, then applies the same *= d; temp += in the same order. Per-lane partials and the subgroupAdd tree
are unchanged, so rows are byte-identical by construction (cell I harness is the judge). Only the generic
mul_mat_vec.comp idg variant with USE_SUBGROUP_ADD_NO_SHMEM gets the path; spec constant 3 (default 0 = old loop).

Lane: lane-302
(cherry picked from commit 323e3a4fc7971a9dc5aa56a485820f5c52f1f337)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-302); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - no served number for this commit in the release ledger or the commit message
